DING GTK 4: avoid cold-boot D-Bus activation storms and 6s SIGKILL livelock.

Upstream DING v105 synchronously introspects org.gnome.Nautilus during
application startup before creating any window, constructs session D-Bus
proxies without DO_NOT_AUTO_START_AT_CONSTRUCTION, unconditionally queries
org.gnome.ArchiveManager1 1s after startup, and kills ding.js with SIGKILL if
all monitor windows do not appear within 6000ms (relaunching it 1ms later).
On cold boot, Live USB, or loaded systems, GTK4/GSK initialization plus
Nautilus/Tracker3/File-Roller activation exceeds 6s and locks the extension in
an infinite SIGKILL/respawn loop with missing desktop icons.

Use bundled introspection XML, defer D-Bus service activation until actual user
operations, guard shutdown relaunches, and remove the destructive 6s SIGKILL
watchdog.

Upstream component: https://gitlab.com/rastersoft/desktop-icons-ng

